# .github/.releaseignore -- dev-only paths for the release gate (gitignore syntax).
# A merged PR whose changed files ALL match here releases nothing, unless it carries a
# semver:* label (an explicit label always wins). Anything not matched is product and
# releases as a patch. Read by .github/workflows/release.yml.
# NOTE git semantics: a file can't be re-included if a parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/**   does NOT work (docs/user/ itself is excluded);
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/  +  !docs/user/**   does.
#
# yt-dlp-mcp specifics: the image is built from go.mod/go.sum, cmd/, internal/
# (non-test) and requirements.txt, and the chart from deploy/helm/ -- all product,
# as are Dockerfile and .dockerignore (they shape the image) and README* (on purpose).
# Nothing under docs/ is embedded, so all of it is dev-only.

# CI, editor and agent config
/.github/
/.devcontainer/
/.claude/
/.vscode/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
/CONTRIBUTING*

# Docs (none are embedded in the binary, image or chart)
/docs/

# Tests and fixtures, including the live smoke test
*_test.go
testdata/
/test/

# Repo and linter config
/.gitignore
/.golangci*
/.pre-commit-config.yaml
/.editorconfig
/.markdownlint*
/.yamllint*
